        {
          "text": "LÜ Kung 呂宮 (T. 長音, 蒼忱, H. 金門), Sept. 28, 1603–1664, May 13, official, was a native of Wu-chin, Kiangnan. He emerged from the examination of 1647 with the rank of optimus or chuang-yüan, being the second scholar to receive that distinction in the Ch'ing dynasty.",
          "source": "eccp-3646136",
